submission.root_cause:
In nvme_trans_inquiry, inq_response is allocated with kmalloc(alloc_len), where alloc_len is the 16-bit ALLOCATION LENGTH taken straight from the attacker-controlled SCSI INQUIRY CDB (can be 0..255 or larger). Several page builders write fixed-size responses into that buffer regardless of alloc_len: the standard inquiry and supported-VPD/serial pages memset/write 36 bytes, the device-identification SCSI-string path writes up to offset 76, and the block-limits page writes and copies 0x3c (60) bytes without clamping to alloc_len. A small alloc_len therefore produces a heap buffer overflow (and kmalloc(0) returns ZERO_SIZE_PTR, which is also written to).</root_cause>
